<!--
  kuna switch self loop: a switch that is its own loop header lost its loop
  in the region structurer.

  GCC and Clang compile `for (;;) switch (next_selector(x)) { ... }` with one
  jump table at the loop head; every case but the default jumps straight back
  to it. P8 structure / RegionStructurer::try_switch_cases treated such a case
  as a continue to an enclosing loop, so folding the switch made its own
  backedge internal and dropped it: the output ran the dispatch once. A
  backedge to the switch itself is now internal to the loop; with no other
  exit the switch is the exit that restores its self-edge, and beside a case
  leaving to another block or restarting an enclosing loop the fold declines
  and the ordinary collapse keeps the loop. Correctness fix, no option: one
  pass pins the loop for both objects of switch_self_loop_x86_64.c (with and
  without leaving cases, and mixed_loop, whose case 4 restarts the enclosing
  loop), for Clang's direct_mixed, whose empty case 0 jumps straight back to
  the dispatch block, and for the hand-written GCC-shaped hoist_dispatch. The
  CLI companion switch_self_loop_cli.rs executes the emitted C against the
  objects.
-->
<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
